@Image1 is the approved aesthetic reference and the exact room: match its two-layer look, marble floor, plaster walls, reception glass, blocky maroon chairs, handless clock and lighting. New camera: first person, seated in one of the blocky maroon chairs in the waiting room, looking across the aisle at the opposite row of identical blocky chairs, the reception glass and receptionist (head down) visible at the side. In the lower frame, two crude blocky four-fingered low-poly hands rest on the lap holding a single small blank white paper slip, a flat untextured quad. All chairs opposite occupied by nothing, perfectly aligned. Cool even light. Perfectly still.

STYLE: Liminal corporate horror. Two rendering layers coexist in one continuous photograph with shared, physically correct lighting. PHOTOREAL LAYER (architecture and matter): floors, walls, glass, marble, light and shadow, 35mm, fine film grain, no grade. LOW-POLY LAYER (anything the company owns): all human figures, furniture, handheld objects, clothing, paper. 1996 PlayStation aesthetic, under 500 triangles, 128x128 textures, affine warping, visible vertex snapping, no anti-aliasing, flat vertex lighting. No compositing seams. No text anywhere.

AVOID: glitch, VHS, scanlines, chromatic aberration, lens flare, bloom, neon, text, watermark, crowds, people other than the receptionist, blood, anime, cartoon, illustration, windows, daylight, sky, stock photo lighting, realistic hands
